Vibe: Industrial-haunted, percussive frostbite, nostalgic decay, terrifyingly innocent.

Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Floor-Tile Hopscotch
- Story & Context: At the exact center of the deserted Sears appliance department, Mallory mapped out a sixty-square grid with yellow caution tape where missing linoleum tiles left raw concrete, daring anyone to step on a crack without triggering the low-frequency hum of the buried floor safe. "Don't look down at the display," she hissed while the arcade cabinet power supply whined into a violent pitch-shift. This opening incident captured the very first night the teenagers successfully routed a desktop xylophone into the mall's public address system.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A cracked linoleum floor in a dark department store illuminated by a single dying fluorescent tube, with a child's chalk hopscotch grid glowing with eerie static energy.

Track 2: The Manager Kept His Teeth in a Dixie Cup
- Story & Context: Hiding inside the employee breakroom of the shuttered Kinney Shoes, Darren confessed to the circle of shivering kids that he had been secretly living off stale pretzels from the Auntie Anne's warming drawer for four months. As the xylophone struck a mocking, child-like cadence in the corridor outside, he pulled a plastic cup from his pocket and emptied a collection of silver fillings onto the linoleum table. "They never stop walking past the storefront," he whispered to the tape recorder, sealing his confession into the static of a rewired cabinet.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A claustrophobic, dark employee breakroom with a rusted metal door, illuminated by the green glow of an exit sign, with a paper cup spilling tiny metallic objects onto a formica table.

Track 3: Whoever Wins the Carousel Loses Sunday
- Story & Context: According to the lore scrawled in greasepencil on the underside of the central atrium escalator, the last person to ride the frozen, headless wooden horses before dawn would be cursed to wander the service tunnels forever as a mall cop. During the climax of their subterranean equinox ritual, the carousel motor suddenly groaned back to life, spinning at a terrifying black-metal velocity while the xylophone player hammered out a frantic, trembling lullaby. "Ride the painted pony straight into the drywall," chanted the crowd as the lights finally blew out for good.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A ghostly, motion-blurred carousel spinning wildly in the middle of a dark, cavernous shopping mall rotunda under a canopy of shattered glass skylights.

